{
  "statement": "To ensure optimal performance efficiency in the RollCall system, my requirements focus on real-time processing, quick response times, and handling a high number of concurrent users. EFF-01 ensures attendance data is processed instantly, while EFF-02 guarantees the system can support at least 500 users simultaneously without degradation. EFF-03 and EFF-05 focus on quick report generation and user record visibility, respectively, both essential for user satisfaction. EFF-06 addresses resource optimization through load balancing. However, I see potential resource conflicts with SafetyAgent's SAF-02 and SAF-03, as real-time data synchronization and automated alerts may introduce latency if not optimized. Additionally, SAF-04 and RES-07's data retention requirements could impact storage efficiency.",
  "conflicts_raised": [
    {
      "ids": ["SAF-02", "EFF-01"],
      "type": "resource",
      "description": "Real-time data synchronization (SAF-02) may conflict with the need for processing attendance data in under 2 seconds (EFF-01) if resources are limited."
    },
    {
      "ids": ["SAF-03", "EFF-03"],
      "type": "resource",
      "description": "Automated alerts for discrepancies (SAF-03) could delay the generation of attendance reports within 5 seconds (EFF-03) if not efficiently managed."
    },
    {
      "ids": ["SAF-04", "RES-07"],
      "type": "resource",
      "description": "Storing historical data for 5 years (SAF-04 and RES-07) may consume significant resources, impacting performance efficiency and data retrieval times."
    }
